.TH COLLIDE 1
.SH NAME
collide \- bouncing-balls 3D physics demo
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wm/collide
.RB [ -cse ]
.RB [ -f ]
.RB [ -op ]
.RB [ -b
.IR num ]
.RB [ -v
.IR num ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Collide
animates a number of balls bouncing and colliding inside a bounding
surface, rendered in 3D.
.TP 10
.B -c
Bound the balls inside a cube.
.TP
.B -s
Bound the balls inside a sphere.
.TP
.B -e
Bound the balls inside an ellipsoid.
.TP
.B -f
Flat-shade the balls instead of the default shading.
.TP
.B -o
Orthographic (no perspective) projection.
.TP
.B -p
An alternate perspective projection.
.TP
.BI -b " num"
Number of balls (also sets the default velocity scale).
.TP
.BI -v " num"
Velocity scale, independent of
.BR -b .
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/wm/collide.b
